            userPrompt: 'Analyze the following survey response:\nSurvey Type: {Survey.type}\nOverall Score: {Survey.overallScore}\nQuestion-Answer Pairs: {Survey.responses}\nOpen Text Answers: {Survey.openTextAnswers}\nContact Custom Properties: {Contact.customProperties}\nPrevious Survey Score: {Contact.previousScore}\nPrevious Respondent Type: {Contact.previousRespondentType}\nSurvey History: {Contact.surveyHistory}\n\nPerform all of the following:\n\n1. Language Detection — Identify the response language from open-text answers.\n\n2. Respondent Classification — Based on {Survey.type} and {Survey.overallScore}, classify the respondent (NPS: Promoter 9-10, Passive 7-8, Detractor 0-6; CSAT: Satisfied 4-5, Neutral 3, Dissatisfied 1-2; CES: Low Effort, Neutral, High Effort).\n\n3. Trend Shift Detection — Compare current classification against {Contact.previousRespondentType} and {Contact.surveyHistory}. Classify as: PROMOTER_TURNED_DETRACTOR, DETRACTOR_TURNED_PROMOTER, CONSISTENT_DETRACTOR, CONSISTENT_PROMOTER, IMPROVING, DECLINING, STABLE, or FIRST_RESPONSE.\n\n4. Topic Extraction & Offering Mapping — Identify every distinct topic mentioned. For each: extract exact phrase, map to {Location.services} or {Location.products}, determine topic-level sentiment, provide quoted snippet, tag survey question origin. Flag RECURRING_ISSUE if same complaint appeared before.\n\n5. Staff / Employee Detection — Identify any staff mentioned. For each: extract reference, match to {Contact.assistedBy}, classify sentiment, flag recurring patterns.\n\n6. Competitor Detection — Identify explicit or implied competitor mentions. For each: extract name or "unnamed competitor", identify comparison aspect, determine if comparison favors competitor, business, or is neutral.\n\n7. Score-Comment Mismatch Detection — Compare quantitative score against open-text sentiment. Flag as: HIGH_SCORE_NEGATIVE_COMMENT, LOW_SCORE_POSITIVE_COMMENT, or ALIGNED.\n\n8. Severity Assessment (Customer-Weighted) — Assess impact considering: score, emotional intensity, specificity, legal/safety mentions, churn-signal language, number of negative topics, competitor comparisons, score-comment mismatch, trend shift, recurring issues. Adjust upward for high-value contacts (enterprise tier, long tenure, high LTV, VIP). Output: severity (LOW | MEDIUM | HIGH | CRITICAL), one-sentence explanation, and escalate=true if CRITICAL or PROMOTER_TURNED_DETRACTOR for a high-value contact.\n\n9. Churn Risk Signal — Determine churn risk: NONE | LOW | MEDIUM | HIGH | IMMINENT.\n\n10. Contact Channel Recommendation — NEGATIVE + MEDIUM or higher: phone + email. NEGATIVE + LOW: email only. POSITIVE or NEUTRAL: no contact. High-value contacts: escalate one level.\n\n11. Personalization Hooks — Extract: customer tenure, last interaction date, segment/tier, prior promoter status, recurring issue context, prior recovery attempts.\n\n12. Advocacy Opportunity — If Promoter/Satisfied AND no score-comment mismatch AND CONSISTENT_PROMOTER or DETRACTOR_TURNED_PROMOTER: flag as eligible for review request or referral. Follow industry-appropriate guidelines for Healthcare or Dental.',
