            userPrompt: 'Write a response to `{Survey.openTextAnswers}` with overall score: `{Survey.overallScore}` (Survey type: `{Survey.type}`).\n\nApply all relevant rules below:\n\nRule 0 — LANGUAGE: Reply in `{survey.language}`. If unavailable, use English.\n\nRule 1 — OPENING: If `{Contact.firstname}` exists, address by first name. If response is older than 7 days, acknowledge delay in the first line. Apply trend-shift-specific openings: PROMOTER_TURNED_DETRACTOR → acknowledge experience fell short of past visits; DETRACTOR_TURNED_PROMOTER → warmly acknowledge the improvement journey; CONSISTENT_PROMOTER → appreciate ongoing loyalty. If `{Survey.hasOpenText}` is false: write 1-2 genuine sentences thanking them for their score, show regret if Detractor, skip topic/staff/competitor sections, go directly to Closing.\n\nRule 2 — TOPIC RESPONSE: Address primary topic first, then negative, then positive, then neutral. Be thankful for positive, empathetic for negative. Use stronger accountability tone for HIGH/CRITICAL severity. If `{survey.recurringIssue}` = true, explicitly acknowledge the issue has come up before and commit to a concrete next step.\n\nRule 3 — SCORE-COMMENT MISMATCH: HIGH_SCORE_NEGATIVE_COMMENT → acknowledge generous score while taking negative feedback seriously. LOW_SCORE_POSITIVE_COMMENT → gently acknowledge appreciation while offering to understand what would have made the experience higher rated.\n\nRule 4 — STAFF: Positive sentiment → mention appreciation will be shared. Negative sentiment → do not name employees, acknowledge concern generally.\n\nRule 5 — COMPETITOR: Never name the competitor. Reinforce your strength on the compared aspect.\n\nRule 6 — CHURN RISK MITIGATION: HIGH or IMMINENT → include clear, personal commitment to resolution and offer direct contact path. MEDIUM → reaffirm investment in the relationship.\n\nRule 7 — ADVOCACY ASK: If `{advocacy_eligible}` = true AND respondent is Promoter/Satisfied AND no score-comment mismatch: invite them to share their experience publicly. Healthcare/Dental: soften to general appreciation invitation.\n\nRule 8 — CONTEXT SIGNALS: Appreciate continued engagement if `{Contact.surveycount}` > 1. Acknowledge long-standing relationship if tenure indicates it. Mention holiday warmly if timestamp matches. Tie in season if relevant.\n\nRule 9 — CLOSING: If `{contact_recommendation.recommend_contact}` = true: invite offline conversation using `{Location.phone}` and/or `{Location.email}`. If `{survey.escalate}` = true: route to senior contact within 24 hours.\n\nRule 10 — TONE BY SURVEY TYPE: NPS Detractor: empathetic, accountable, action-oriented. NPS Promoter: appreciative, relationship-reinforcing. CSAT low: focused on the specific transaction. CES high-effort: acknowledge friction explicitly. Pulse/short-form: keep response proportionally brief.\n\nRule 11 — LENGTH: Score-only response: 2-3 sentences. Standard with open-text: 4-7 sentences. High-severity or churn-risk: up to 9 sentences, never feel templated.\n\nAfter applying all rules, finalize the message by performing necessary translation to match `{survey.language}`.',
